1. Witchcraft (Dropbox, Inc.)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:  https://github.com/dropbox/witchcraft
License: Apache License 2.0
Copyright: Copyright (c) Dropbox, Inc. and the Witchcraft authors.

Switchcraft is a Swift port of Witchcraft, the Rust reimplementation of
XTR-Warp. Algorithmic structure, the LSM-tree indexer layout, the k-means
training loop, the Q4 residual codec, the index-key compression scheme, the
hybrid RRF fusion strategy, the sliding-window long-input embedder, and
several configuration constants are derived from upstream Witchcraft. Files
that contain ported logic preserve inline "Port of upstream Witchcraft"
attributions (see, in particular, Sources/SwitchcraftCore/KMeans/KMeans.swift,
Sources/SwitchcraftCore/Indexer/{Indexer,IndexerConfig,IndicesCodec}.swift,
Sources/SwitchcraftCore/Search/{SearchEngine,SearchConfig,HybridConfig}.swift,
Sources/SwitchcraftCore/Codec/Q4Codec.swift,
Sources/SwitchcraftCore/Embedding/StoreConfig.swift, and
Sources/SwitchcraftCoreML/{SlidingWindow,T5CoreMLEmbedder}.swift).

------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. google/xtr-base-en
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:  https://huggingface.co/google/xtr-base-en
License: Apache License 2.0
Copyright: Copyright (c) Google LLC.

Switchcraft's reference Embedder (`SwitchcraftCoreML.T5CoreMLEmbedder`)
loads the `google/xtr-base-en` T5 encoder and `2_Dense/` projection layer,
converted to a CoreML `.mlpackage` by `scripts/convert-xtr-to-coreml.py`.
The model architecture, weights, and projection layer are governed by the
upstream Apache 2.0 license. The `.mlpackage` asset is built locally and
not redistributed in this repository.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. HuggingFace tokenizers
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:  https://github.com/huggingface/tokenizers
License: Apache License 2.0
Copyright: Copyright (c) HuggingFace, Inc. and the tokenizers authors.

Switchcraft's `Tokenizer` (Sources/SwitchcraftCore/Tokenizer/) is a Swift
port of the HuggingFace `tokenizers` Unigram (SentencePiece) pipeline. The
`tokenizer.json` schema, the Unigram lattice algorithm, the added-tokens
pre-segmentation pass, the Precompiled normalizer's double-array trie, and
the BPE/Unigram/Decoder/PostProcessor pipeline match upstream semantics.
Files that contain ported logic preserve inline attributions (see, in
particular, Sources/SwitchcraftCore/Tokenizer/{Tokenizer,UnigramModel,
AddedTokens,DoubleArrayTrie,Normalizer,PreTokenizer,PostProcessor,
Decoder}.swift).
